  {
    "chunk": "Question answering (QA) is a computer science discipline within the fields of information retrieval and natural language processing (NLP) that is concerned with building systems that automatically answer questions that are posed by humans in a natural language. [1]\nOverview\nA question-answering implementation, usually a computer program, may construct its answers by querying a structured database of knowledge or information, usually a knowledge base. More commonly, question-answering systems can pull answers from an unstructured collection of natural language documents.",
    "summary": "Question answering (QA) involves creating systems to automatically answer human questions using structured or unstructured data.",
    "question": "What is the purpose of question answering systems?",
